de></pre><h2 id=3D"retrieving-the-expected-count-of-a-query-results">Retrie=
ving the Expected Count of a Query Results</h2>
<p>If you'd like to know the expected count of the results of the query you=
 can add the
<code>Hyland-Include-Item-Count</code> custom request header to this reques=
t. The value of this
header should be set to <code>true</code> if you would like the expected co=
unt to be included in
the custom response header <code>Hyland-Item-Count</code>. If the <code>Hyl=
and-Include-Item-Count</code>
header value is set to <code>false</code>, or if the header is left off the=
 request, the
<code>Hyland-Item-Count</code> header will not be included on the response.=
</p>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">POST</span> <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-string">/documents/queries</span> HTTP/1.1
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Type</span>: application/json
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Hyland-Include-Item-Count</span>: true

<span class=3D"json">{
  <span class=3D"hljs-attr">"queryType"</span>: [
    {
      <span class=3D"hljs-attr">"type"</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-string">=
"CustomQuery"</span>,
      <span class=3D"hljs-attr">"ids"</span>: [<span class=3D"hljs-string">=
"121"</span>]
    }
  ]
}</span></code></pre><pre class=3D"hljs"><code>HTTP/1.1 <span class=3D"hljs=
-number">201</span> Created
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Type</span>: application/json
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Location</span>: {hostName}/documents/querie=
s/{queryId}/results
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Hyland-Item-Count</span>: 10

<span class=3D"json">{
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">"id"</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-string">"{qu=
eryId}"</span>
}</span></code></pre><h3 id=3D"curl-example">curl example</h3>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code>curl POST https://localhost/apiserver/onbase/core=
/documents/queries -H <span class=3D"hljs-string">"Authorization: Bearer {t=
oken}"</span> -H <span class=3D"hljs-string">"Content-Type: application/jso=
n"</span> -H <span class=3D"hljs-string">"Hyland-Include-Item-Count: true"<=
/span> -d <span class=3D"hljs-string">"{\"</span>queryType\<span class=3D"h=
ljs-string">": [{\"</span><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">type</span>\<span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-string">": \"</span>CustomQuery\<span class=3D"hljs-string">", =
\"</span>ids\<span class=3D"hljs-string">": [\"</span><span class=3D"hljs-n=
umber">121</span>\<span class=3D"hljs-string">"]}]}"</span></code></pre><p>=
The count included in the <code>Hyland-Item-Count</code> header is an estim=
ate. When retrieving the
actual results you might not get the same number. Additionally, adding
<code>Hyland-Include-Item-Count</code> will incur additional performance ov=
erhead when executing this
request. If the <code>/documents/queries/{queryId}/results</code> endpoint =
will generally be called
immediately after this, then including this header is not recommended. Inst=
ead, the accurate
count can be calculated based on the response from the <code>/documents/que=
ries/{queryId}/results</code>
endpoint and the <code>/documents/queries</code> endpoint will not have to =
experience decreased
performance. The use of <code>Hyland-Include-Item-Count</code> can be very =
helpful if retrieving the full
results of the query may not be done immediately or ever at all.</p>
<h2 id=3D"retrieving-a-query's-results">Retrieving a Query's Results</h2>
<p>Once you have the id of a query, you can retrieve the document results o=
f this query.
This is done by performing a GET on <code>/documents/queries/{queryId}/resu=
lts</code>, which is
the url that will be included in the Location header of the POST response o=
f
<code>/documents/queries</code>.</p>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">GET</span> <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-string">/documents/queries/{queryId}/results</span> HTTP/1.1</co=
de></pre><pre class=3D"hljs"><code>HTTP/1.1 <span class=3D"hljs-number">200=
</span> Ok
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Type</span>: application/json

<span class=3D"json">{
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">"items"</span>: [
        {
            <span class=3D"hljs-attr">"displayColumns"</span>: [
                {
